{"id":"private-centres-public-money","title":"Privately owned centres and public money","question":"Which privately owned centres does public money reach, by which route, and do any draw on several streams for the same places?","finding":"31 privately owned centre operators (companies, individual licensees and corporations with no tax-exempt record found) are attached to at least one public stream; 27 of them, with 2,900 licensed places, are on the City's list of funded centres, the largest being Bright Horizons Children's Center, LLC with 821 places, and 10 draw on two or more streams. None holds a State contract and none is paid by the City's early-childhood departments by name: what each receives is paid through the two referral agencies, whose returns name only their five largest payees a year. The City's voucher table names 5 of them as direct payees, $194,344 in all; for 4 the payment is booked to a Human Services Agency wage-subsidy account, not to a child-care account. Separately, early-childhood departments paid $19.9 million to payees the voucher table does not name at all (\"Single Payment Payees\").","how":"An operator is treated as privately owned when the licensee is a limited-liability company or partnership, an individual, or a corporation whose name is not on the federal list of tax-exempt organizations and that the City does not flag as a nonprofit. Streams: the City list of funded centres (by licence number), the City list of agencies receiving its salary grant for early educators (August 2026, name match), the State's meal-programme site list (by address), facilities grants named on the Low Income Investment Fund's tax returns (name match), State contracts and Head Start. Direct City payments are payments in the voucher table to a payee whose name equals the licensee or centre name; the purpose is the account the City booked them to. The registration date is the earliest start date of a business registered with the City under the same name.","limits":"The City's own list of funded centres includes companies and nonprofits alike, and its published rate sheet gives one rate per child for centres and homes. Being on the list says nothing about how much a centre is paid or for how many children; the City publishes neither. A corporation not found on the federal tax-exempt list may still be a nonprofit filing under another name or exempt as a church. Name matches between the licence file, the payment file and the business register can be wrong in both directions. Individual licensees are not named; their centres are, as the City's own list names them. The record that would show the amounts is the referral agencies' provider payment ledgers. The payment file labels each line with a fiscal year that is not always the year the payment was issued: some earlier payments, mostly on purchase orders in multi-year capital funds, are filed under a later year, and the Controller's own published figures follow that label. Payments are dated here by voucher number, a single running sequence, which moves $5.52 billion of $119.3 billion (4.6%) to an earlier year than its label; $1.08 billion of that belongs to fiscal 2018 or earlier, before the file starts. Near the turn of a year the number dates a payment to within a few days.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"centre","t":"Centre","type":"text"},{"k":"operator","t":"Operator","type":"org"},{"k":"kind","t":"Kind of operator","type":"text"},{"k":"licences","t":"Open licences","type":"int"},{"k":"places","t":"Licensed places","type":"int"},{"k":"cityNetwork","t":"Licences on the City list of funded centres","type":"int"},{"k":"salaryGrant","t":"City salary grant for educators","type":"text"},{"k":"mealSite","t":"Federal meal programme","type":"text"},{"k":"facilitiesGrant","t":"Facilities grants","type":"usd"},{"k":"facilitiesYears","t":"Tax years","type":"text"},{"k":"cityDirect","t":"Paid directly by the City","type":"usd"},{"k":"cityDirectYears","t":"Fiscal years","type":"text"},{"k":"cityDirectFor","t":"Booked as","type":"text"},{"k":"seriousCitations","t":"Most serious citations","type":"int"},{"k":"upheld","t":"Complaint allegations upheld","type":"int"},{"k":"registered","t":"Business registered (name match)","type":"date"},{"k":"since","t":"First licensed","type":"date"},{"k":"streams","t":"Public streams","type":"int"},{"k":"which","t":"Which","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"centre":"Little Footprints Preschool Oceanview; Little Footprints Preschool, Corp.","operator":"Little Footprints Preschool, Corp.","operatorKey":null,"kind":"Corporation, tax status not found","licences":2,"places":184,"cityNetwork":2,"salaryGrant":"Yes","mealSite":null,"facilitiesGrant":37540,"facilitiesYears":"2021","cityDirect":20011,"cityDirectYears":"2021–2023","cityDirectFor":"Non-CalWorks Wage Subsidy, Extended Sick Leave Benefits","seriousCitations":null,"upheld":null,"registered":"2016-11-01","since":"2011-04-30","streams":3,"which":"City network of funded centres, City salary grant for educators, facilities grant"},{"centre":"Little Robles In The Sunset","operator":"Little Robles Irving LLC","operatorKey":null,"kind":"Private company","licences":1,"places":45,"cityNetwork":1,"salaryGrant":"Yes","mealSite":null,"facilitiesGrant":235490,"facilitiesYears":"2023, 2024","cityDirect":null,"cityDirectYears":null,"cityDirectFor":null,"seriousCitations":1,"upheld":null,"registered":"2021-12-20","since":"2023-03-29","streams":3,"which":"City network of funded centres, City salary grant for educators, facilities grant"},{"centre":"L'academy Language Immersion Preschool SF CPMC PS; L'academy Preschool Mission Noe; L'academy Preschool SF Hayes Valley; L'academy Preschool SF Nob Hill; L'acad","operator":"Immersion 5 LLC","operatorKey":null,"kind":"Private company","licences":9,"places":541,"cityNetwork":6,"salaryGrant":"Yes","mealSite":null,"facilitiesGrant":null,"facilitiesYears":null,"cityDirect":null,"cityDirectYears":null,"cityDirectFor":null,"seriousCitations":1